[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Mill_Labhint DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="Nurse Trimble"
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="Trimble is the real brains behind the Mill operation. He only leaves the Geezer to attend his lab experiments."

[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Mill_Mechanichint DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="Hatter Mechanic in Sewer"
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="The Hatter mechanic has not returned from trying to restore the water in the sewers. He knows the combination to the engine room."

[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Sewer_MaintKey DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="Hatter Mechanic Apt Key"
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="The Hatter Mechanic's key opens the locker in his apartment, located in Drapers Ward Streets."

[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Ship_Drowning DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="A drowned victim"
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="The mutineer Edgar Wakefield has drowned a gang member that was loyal to Lizzy, and sank him in the river near the Undine."

[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Ship_EdgarLives DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="Mercy for a Traitor"
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="You kept Edgar Wakefield alive when you had every reason to kill him. This mercy has not gone unnoticed."

[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Ship_EngineCoil DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="The Stolen Engine Coil"
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="The Hatters have stolen the Engine Coil from the Dead Eel's ship the Undine. The ship is inoperable without it. It must be recovered before Lizzy can take you up the river to the Brigmore Manor."

[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Ship_ScoutSpotted DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="Scout Spotted"
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="A mysterious figure was seen scouting the Undine and her crew, but they teleported away before you could investigate further."

[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Street_DressMaker DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="The Dressmaker"
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="The dressmaker in Drapers Ward once crafted upscale clothing for Emily Kaldwin, heir to the throne."

[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Street_GangWar DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="Gang War"
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="The Dead Eels and the Hatters are engaged in a full scale gang war."

[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Street_Granny DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="Granny's Recipe"
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="Granny Rags prepared a renewal of her vows to the Outsider. Complete the ritual to collect the wedding gift."

[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Street_Jerome DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="Jerome the Black Market Merchant"
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="A former merchant from Drapers Ward's better days, Jerome now deals in black market and hard-to-find items from the safety of his apartment overlooking Millinery Canal."

[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Street_Oxrush DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="The Oxrush Flower"
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="The rare Oxrush flower is prized for its medicinal and alchemical properties."

[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Street_Password DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="Hatter's Mill Password"
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="The Hatters have a secret password they use to gain entry to the Textile Mill that serves as their base."

[DrapersWard.Chapternotes_Street_Skinflint DisAbstractItem]
m_ItemName="Skinflint is a deadbeat."
m_PluralItemName=""
m_Description="The Hatter known as Skinflint has never paid Jerome for the goods he took. Skinflint is a chain smoker charged with guarding the sewer door near the canal."

